# Pixels of gpu/lines' dump that are not compared (FORMAT.md,
# "Exclusions"; docs/conformance.md, "Excluded pixels (`lines`)").
#
# gouraudMultiLine sets the colours of vertices 0, 1 and 2 (setRGB2 twice)
# and never vertex 3's, so the console drew the last segment of each
# Gouraud polyline towards whatever its stack held there; the recorder
# sends 0 (docs/testing.md, "Conformance tests and the recorder").
# Each run is the segment from vertex 2 at (x + 32, 172) back to vertex 3
# at (x, 140) without its first pixel, which has vertex 2's colour.
run 181 171 -1 -1 32  last segment of the opaque Gouraud polyline: vertex 3's colour never set
run 241 171 -1 -1 32  last segment of the semi-transparent Gouraud polyline: vertex 3's colour never set
